{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"disgusting-natatory-blackrhino","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context / Problem\nReconciler parity bugs (3f04, 4b59, 32cc class: inverted link directions, asymmetric field handling) escape because per-field asymmetry POLICY (add-wins tags, should_propagate_removal gates) lives only in code, and pagination loops are hand-rolled at multiple call sites (acli_graph.py carries triple token loops). The typed-transport half of this hardening is already in flight as bug cc77 (in_progress) — do not duplicate it.\n\n## Approach\n(1) Property tests pinning the DECLARED per-field asymmetry policy as executable fixtures: for each field in the contract, its declared symmetry class (bidirectional-roundtrip / add-wins / one-way with propagation gate) is asserted by a parameterized property test; roundtrip identity asserted ONLY for value codecs of genuinely bidirectional fields (status mapping, link inward/outward direction). (2) One paged-iterator per pagination PROTOCOL (offset=DC, token=Cloud-v3) following fetcher._iter_pages; migrate acli_graph.py token loops onto it; call sites never hand-loop. Precedent: pycontribs _fetch_pages / go-jira SearchPages.\n\n## Scope\n- tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/: new property test module over the field contract\n- src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/adapters/jira/acli_graph.py + fetcher.py iterator consolidation\n\n## Testing\nProperty tests are themselves the deliverable for (1); for (2), existing pagination tests must pass through the shared iterator, plus one test per protocol proving multi-page traversal and terminal-page handling.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Every contract field's symmetry class is pinned by a property test; changing a policy breaks a test naming the field.\n- [ ] Roundtrip identity is asserted only for declared-bidirectional value codecs.\n- [ ] acli_graph.py contains zero hand-rolled pagination loops; both protocols route through shared iterators with tests.\n- [ ] relates_to link recorded to cc77 (typed transport, separate in-flight work).","id":"e931-7f1f-8b0c-465b","parent_id":"2f4c-7e5c-e782-4e97","priority":2,"tags":["reconciler"],"ticket_type":"story","title":"Reconciler: declared-asymmetry property tests + pagination iterator dedup"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1785640092677590001,"uuid":"4b3e4992-17c1-42ea-a9e5-82d4b146bc97"}